  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>tr_threshold_sweep - prices nine flagging thresholds against the confirmed outcomes, to choose the one
that costs least.
Run on its own, by hand; needs transaction_scores (Credit Card) and confirmed_outcomes
(tr_load_outcomes).
Parameters: COST_MISSED_FRAUD (200), COST_REVIEW (25).

1. tbl-scores_and_outcomes: Table input, transaction_scores joined to confirmed_outcomes.
2. dg-thresholds: Data grid, nine thresholds from 0.02 to 0.5; gv-costs: Get variables, the two costs.
3. jr-every_threshold: Join rows, every transaction with every threshold (main step: the table input).
4. frmla-outcome_at_threshold: Formula, tp, fp and fn as 1 or 0.
5. sort-threshold, grp-threshold: Sort rows and Group by threshold, the sums.
6. frmla-precision_recall_cost: Formula, flagged, precision_rate, recall_rate and cost.
7. sv-format: Select values, Meta-data tab, the formats.
8. txt-threshold_report: Text file output, output/threshold_report.csv; wlog-threshold_report: Write to log.

Shipped data: at 0.5 cost 17950 and recall_rate 0.2130; the cheapest is 0.15, cost 16175, recall_rate 0.3981.</note>
      <xloc>96</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>628</width>
      <heigth>296</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>167</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>224</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>245</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>100</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>100</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>100</bordercolorblue>
      <drawshadow>Y</drawshadow>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
